record akr.evidence.handoff-guidance-single-source/1 : evidence {
    title "The handoff brief is four lines, authored in one file, with no second prose copy"
    state verified
    result pass
    method manual
    observed_at git:9579d4eed67ed1128c18ccbb349f8bafeaee8c2a
    summary """
        The agent-facing handoff brief exists once, in scripts/agent-section.md, at four lines: three command sentences naming worker, scout, advisor and reviewer; one reason line of exactly ten words (Because inherited facts are cheap and inherited conclusions are not); and one pointer to akr handoff --help. AGENTS.md carries the same four lines because it is an install target of that file, not a second authored copy, and adds one sentence telling a reader not to restate the detail there. docs/08-mcp.md section 8 embeds the same text verbatim, which is what that section is for. The Claude skill file .claude/skills/handoff/SKILL.md, which held a fifth copy of the workflow as prose, is deleted rather than trimmed. Verified by reading all four files after the change; the previous wave's long Calling an advisor block appears in none of them.
        """
    author "GitHub Uploader"
}

record akr.evidence.handoff-transport-suite/1 : evidence {
    title "756 tests passed across 58 binaries, including the thirteen handoff cases and the MCP differential"
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:9579d4eed67ed1128c18ccbb349f8bafeaee8c2a
    command "cargo test"
    summary """
        The whole suite ran at 9579d4e with no failures. New coverage: crates/akr-cli/tests/handoff.rs (thirteen cases, the load-bearing ones negative — worker discloses the parent's notes while scout, reviewer and advisor do not; a packet resolves the capsule rather than a copy of it, proved by correcting the capsule and re-reading an earlier packet; the session request survives newlines and quotes and a narrowing renders beneath it rather than in place of it; coverage names what a child declared unopened and no child read, and stops naming it once somebody does; akr start reports an open session and, under AKR_HANDOFF_PACKET, names the packet to open instead) and a_handoff_opens_the_same_way_from_either_surface in the MCP differential, which also proves opening over MCP does not stamp the packet and that the coverage roll-up matches from either side. One earlier run of the same suite failed to build rather than to test, because concurrent akr invocations held target/debug/akr.exe on Windows; re-run clean.
        """
    author "GitHub Uploader"
}

